## Feature 3: Unified Media Gallery, Filtering, Sorting & Multi-View Display

### 3.1 Overview & Architecture
The Gallery engine provides a consolidated, reactive media canvas capable of presenting heterogeneous data types (images, videos, documents) within a single unified view. It features client-side full-text search, category segmenting, multi-property sorting, and three responsive layout renderers: Grid, List, and Masonry.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Data Hydration
        A1["fetchImages()"] --> B["Promise.all()"]
        A2["fetchVideos()"] --> B
        A3["fetchDocuments()"] --> B
        B --> C["Merge & Map mediaType: 'image'|'video'|'document'"]
    end

    subgraph Data Pipeline
        C --> D["allMedia Array"]
        D --> E{"Category Filter Tab"}
        E -- 'all' --> F["All Media"]
        E -- 'images' --> F["Only Images"]
        E -- 'videos' --> F["Only Videos"]
        E -- 'documents' --> F["Only Documents"]
        
        F --> G["Search Filter (searchQuery on originalName)"]
        G --> H["Sort Engine (sortBy: date/name/size/type & sortOrder: asc/desc)"]
        H --> I["filteredMedia Array"]
    end

    subgraph Rendering Layouts
        I --> J{"viewMode State"}
        J -- 'grid' --> K["CSS Grid (Uniform 4:3 Aspect Thumbnails)"]
        J -- 'list' --> L["Tabular Rows (Name, Size, Type, Date, Actions)"]
        J -- 'masonry' --> M["Column Waterfall (Variable Height Cards)"]
    end
```

### 3.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Polymorphic Data Merging
Because images, videos, and documents possess dedicated MongoDB collections with slight schema variances (e.g., videos feature `duration` and `thumbnail`; documents feature `type`), the client-side controller in `ImageUploadPage.js` synthesizes them into a unified array:
```javascript
const allMedia = [
  ...images.map(img => ({ ...img, mediaType: 'image' })),
  ...videos.map(vid => ({ ...vid, mediaType: 'video' })),
  ...documents.map(doc => ({ ...doc, mediaType: 'document' })),
].sort((a, b) => new Date(b.uploadDate || b.createdAt) - new Date(a.uploadDate || a.createdAt));
```
This synthesized structure allows downstream components (`ImageGallery`, `SkeletonGrid`, `BottomDock`) to interact with media items via common properties (`_id`, `originalName`, `size`, `uploadDate`, `folder`, `mediaType`).

#### Multi-Tier Filtering & Search Optimization
Data filtering is executed in memory via a memoized multi-pass pipeline. The first tier inspects `activeCategory`: when set to `'images'`, `'videos'`, or `'documents'`, it performs strict equality checks against `item.mediaType`. The second tier executes real-time string filtering:
```javascript
item.originalName?.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase())
```
Because the filtering occurs on cached React state, the user experiences zero-latency search feedback without triggering database round-trips.

#### The Multi-Criteria Comparator Engine
Sorting is dynamically configured through two independent state variables: `sortBy` (`'date'` | `'name'` | `'size'` | `'type'`) and `sortOrder` (`'asc'` | `'desc'`). A unified comparator function evaluates item pairs `(a, b)`:
- **Date**: Computes delta between epoch timestamps: `new Date(b.uploadDate) - new Date(a.uploadDate)`.
- **Name**: Executes locale-aware string comparison: `a.originalName.localeCompare(b.originalName)`.
- **Size**: Compares raw byte numbers: `(a.size || 0) - (b.size || 0)`.
- **Type**: Evaluates MIME/extension strings alphabetically.

The boolean direction toggle inverts the computed comparator sign, ensuring consistent order transitions across all four sort dimensions.

#### Layout Renderers: Grid, List, and Masonry
`ImageGallery.js` switches its DOM layout based on `viewMode`:
1. **Grid View (`.image-grid`)**: Configured with CSS Grid (`grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))`). Media cards render with a uniform 4:3 aspect ratio thumbnail container. Hovering over a card activates an action overlay revealing quick buttons for Preview, Download, Share, and Delete.
2. **List View (`.media-list-view`)**: Renders a dense, table-like layout. Each row features a small thumbnail icon, the filename, human-readable file size, creation timestamp, and right-aligned action buttons. This view maximizes vertical screen real estate for organizational workflows.
3. **Masonry View (`.media-masonry-view`)**: Employs CSS multi-column layouts (`column-count: 4; column-gap: 16px`, scaling down to 3, 2, and 1 on smaller screens). Child cards set `break-inside: avoid`. Images preserve their intrinsic aspect ratios without cropping, providing an artistic presentation for photography collections.

