## Feature 5: In-Browser Image Editing Studio

### 5.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub includes a studio-grade, client-side image editor implemented in `ImageEditor.js`. Users can crop arbitrary rectangular regions, perform geometric transformations (rotation, horizontal/vertical flipping), adjust color matrices (brightness, contrast, saturation, sepia, blur), apply one-click stylized filter presets, and render the final composite to HTML5 Canvas for non-destructive storage.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Raw Image Element (imgRef)"] --> B["Active Editing Tool"]
    
    subgraph Editing Toolsets
        B -- "Crop Tool" --> C["react-image-crop UI Overlay"]
        B -- "Transform Tool" --> D["Rotation (90° steps) & Flip H/V"]
        B -- "Filter Tool" --> E["Presets & 5 Parametric Sliders"]
    end
    
    C --> F["Update crop / completedCrop State"]
    D --> G["Update rotation, flipH, flipV State"]
    E --> H["Update filters CSS String"]
    
    F & G & H --> I["Real-Time CSS Transform & Filter Preview on DOM"]
    
    I --> J["User Clicks 'Save as Copy'"]
    
    subgraph Canvas Rendering Pipeline
        J --> K["Compute Source Coordinates (sx, sy, sWidth, sHeight)"]
        K --> L["Handle 90°/270° Canvas Dimension Swapping"]
        L --> M["ctx.translate(canvas.width/2, canvas.height/2)"]
        M --> N["ctx.rotate(rotation * PI / 180)"]
        N --> O["ctx.scale(flipH, flipV)"]
        O --> P["ctx.filter = filterStyle"]
        P --> Q["ctx.drawImage(img, sx, sy, sWidth, sHeight, -sWidth/2, -sHeight/2, sWidth, sHeight)"]
    end
    
    Q --> R["canvas.toBlob('image/png')"]
    R --> S["Encapsulate in FormData (filename: edited-name.png)"]
    S --> T["POST /api/images/upload (Bearer Auth)"]
    T --> U["Image Added to Gallery & Activity Logged"]
```

### 5.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Crop Engine (`react-image-crop`)
Cropping is integrated using the `react-image-crop` library. When the user activates the Crop tool, the image is wrapped in a `<ReactCrop>` container that captures mouse and touch gestures. When the user finishes dragging the crop box, it sets `completedCrop`. To ensure pixel-accurate output regardless of screen scaling or responsive CSS resizing, the save routine calculates a dimensional scaling ratio:
```javascript
const scaleX = img.naturalWidth / img.width;
const scaleY = img.naturalHeight / img.height;
const sx = completedCrop.x * scaleX;
const sy = completedCrop.y * scaleY;
const sWidth = completedCrop.width * scaleX;
const sHeight = completedCrop.height * scaleY;
```

#### Parametric Filters & Preset Matrix
The filter engine supports eight custom presets and five granular sliders:
- **Filter Presets**: `None`, `Vivid` (110% brightness, 120% contrast, 140% saturation), `Warm` (sepia 20%), `Cool` (saturation 80%), `B&W` (grayscale 100%), `Vintage` (sepia 40%, contrast 90%), `Dramatic` (contrast 150%, brightness 90%), and `Soft` (blur 1px).
- **Manual Sliders**: Brightness (0–200%), Contrast (0–200%), Saturation (0–200%), Sepia (0–100%), and Blur (0–10px).

These values are compiled into a standards-compliant CSS filter string:
```javascript
const filterStyle = `brightness(${filters.brightness}%) contrast(${filters.contrast}%) saturate(${filters.saturate}%) grayscale(${filters.grayscale}%) sepia(${filters.sepia}%) blur(${filters.blur}px)`;
```
This filter string is applied live to the preview DOM element for zero-latency interactive feedback.

#### The Canvas 2D Rendering Pipeline
When saving, a hidden `<canvas ref={canvasRef}>` executes the export sequence:
1. **Dimension Resolution**: If the image is rotated by an odd multiple of 90 degrees (`rotation % 180 !== 0`), canvas width and height are inverted: `canvas.width = sHeight; canvas.height = sWidth`.
2. **Context Coordinate Transformation**: The canvas context is translated to its exact center point: `ctx.translate(canvas.width / 2, canvas.height / 2)`.
3. **Rotational & Mirror Matrix**: The canvas rotates: `ctx.rotate((rotation * Math.PI) / 180)` and scales: `ctx.scale(flipH ? -1 : 1, flipV ? -1 : 1)`.
4. **Hardware Filter Injection**: `ctx.filter = filterStyle` applies the exact visual adjustments.
5. **Draw Image Execution**: `ctx.drawImage` draws the source crop rectangle offset by negative half-dimensions: `(-sWidth / 2, -sHeight / 2)`.

#### Non-Destructive Export & Re-Ingestion
The populated canvas executes `canvas.toBlob((blob) => { ... }, 'image/png')`. The resulting binary blob is packaged into a `FormData` object with the filename formatted as `edited-${image.originalName}`. It is transmitted to `POST /api/images/upload` using the active user's JWT token. The original source image is preserved intact, ensuring non-destructive image authoring.

