## Feature 6: Folder Management, Hierarchical Organization & Drag-and-Drop

### 6.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub provides a flexible folder organization system allowing users to categorize assets into custom-named, color-coded directories. It features compound unique indexing, dynamic file counting across collections, fluid HTML5 drag-and-drop file organization, and safe folder deletion that unfiles assets without destroying data.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User Interface
    participant FolderAPI as /api/folders
    participant FolderModel as Folder Model
    participant MediaModel as Image / Video / Document Models
    participant DB as MongoDB Atlas

    Note over User,DB: Folder Creation with Color & Unique Name
    User->>FolderAPI: POST /api/folders { name: "Travel 2026", color: "#34a853" }
    FolderAPI->>FolderModel: Folder.create({ name, color, user: req.user.id })
    alt Duplicate Name for User
        FolderModel-->>FolderAPI: MongoError E11000 (duplicate key)
        FolderAPI-->>User: 400 Bad Request { message: 'A folder with this name already exists' }
    else Success
        FolderModel->>DB: Save document
        FolderAPI-->>User: 201 Created (Folder object with zero counts)
    end

    Note over User,DB: Drag-and-Drop File Relocation
    User->>FolderAPI: PUT /api/folders/:id/move { fileIds: ["img123"], fileType: "image" }
    FolderAPI->>MediaModel: Image.updateMany({ _id: { $in: fileIds }, user }, { folder: folderId })
    MediaModel->>DB: Update documents
    FolderAPI-->>User: 200 OK { message: 'Files moved to folder' }

    Note over User,DB: Safe Folder Deletion (Unfiling Assets)
    User->>FolderAPI: DELETE /api/folders/:id
    FolderAPI->>MediaModel: Image.updateMany({ folder: id }, { folder: null })
    FolderAPI->>MediaModel: Video.updateMany({ folder: id }, { folder: null })
    FolderAPI->>MediaModel: Document.updateMany({ folder: id }, { folder: null })
    FolderAPI->>FolderModel: folder.deleteOne()
    FolderModel->>DB: Remove folder entity
    FolderAPI-->>User: 200 OK { message: 'Folder deleted' }
```

### 6.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Schema Architecture & Compound Indexing
In `backend/models/Folder.js`, the schema defines `name`, `color` (defaulting to Google Blue `#4285f4`), `user` (foreign key pointing to User), and `sharedWith` array. To guarantee that a user cannot create two folders with identical names while permitting different users to use the same name, a compound unique index is enforced:
```javascript
folderSchema.index({ name: 1, user: 1 }, { unique: true });
```
When a duplicate occurs, Mongoose raises an error with code `11000`, which the route handler catches and translates into a friendly `400 Bad Request` response.

#### Parallel Cross-Collection Count Aggregation
When the client calls `GET /api/folders`, the server does not simply return raw folder records. It aggregates the quantity of images, videos, and documents residing inside each folder using `Promise.all`:
```javascript
const foldersWithCounts = await Promise.all(
  folders.map(async (folder) => {
    const [imageCount, videoCount, docCount] = await Promise.all([
      Image.countDocuments({ folder: folder._id, user: req.user.id }),
      Video.countDocuments({ folder: folder._id, user: req.user.id }),
      Document.countDocuments({ folder: folder._id, user: req.user.id }),
    ]);
    return {
      ...folder.toObject(),
      fileCount: imageCount + videoCount + docCount,
      imageCount,
      videoCount,
      docCount,
    };
  })
);
```
This enables the UI to render rich metadata badges (e.g., "12 files · 8 📷 · 3 🎥 · 1 📄") on every folder card.

#### HTML5 Drag-and-Drop Mechanics
GalleryHub implements native HTML5 drag-and-drop. In `ImageGallery.js`, media cards specify `draggable="true"`. On `dragStart`, the card writes a serialized JSON payload to the data transfer buffer:
```javascript
e.dataTransfer.setData('application/json', JSON.stringify({ id: item._id, mediaType: item.mediaType }));
```
Both the "Quick Folders" carousel on the dashboard and the full folder list in the Folders tab act as drop targets. They listen for `onDragOver` (invoking `e.preventDefault()` to permit dropping and adding the CSS class `.drop-highlight`) and `onDrop`. On drop, the folder extracts the ID and mediaType, and dispatches a call to `handleMoveToFolder(folder._id, id, mediaType)`.

#### Safe Deletion & Cascade Unfiling
Deleting a folder does not delete the files contained inside it. When `DELETE /api/folders/:id` executes, it initiates three parallel unfiling operations:
```javascript
await Promise.all([
  Image.updateMany({ folder: folder._id }, { folder: null }),
  Video.updateMany({ folder: folder._id }, { folder: null }),
  Document.updateMany({ folder: folder._id }, { folder: null }),
]);
await folder.deleteOne();
```
All assets contained in the deleted directory automatically revert to root unfiled files in the user's gallery.

