## Feature 7: Collaborative Folder Sharing & Role-Based Access Control

### 7.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub allows users to share entire folders with other registered platform users. The folder collaboration system implements role-based access control (RBAC), dividing permissions into Viewer (read-only) and Editor (read/write) access levels.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Folder Owner opens ShareFolderModal"] --> B["Enter Collaborator Email & Select Role ('view' | 'edit')"]
    B --> C["POST /api/folders/:id/share"]
    
    C --> D{"Validation Checks"}
    D -- Target User Not Found --> E["404: User not found"]
    D -- Target == Owner --> F["400: Cannot share with yourself"]
    D -- Already Shared --> G["Update Permission Level in sharedWith Array"]
    D -- New User --> H["Push { user: targetId, permission } to sharedWith"]
    
    G & H --> I["folder.save() & Return Updated Collaborator Roster"]
    
    subgraph Shared View Experience
        J["Invited Collaborator logs in"] --> K["GET /api/folders/shared"]
        K --> L["Query: Folder.find({ 'sharedWith.user': req.user.id })"]
        L --> M["Populate Owner Info (name, email)"]
        M --> N["Aggregate File Counts for Shared Folder"]
        N --> O["Inject myPermission ('view' | 'edit') and isShared: true"]
        O --> P["Render in Shared Folders Gallery View"]
    end
```

### 7.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Schema Subdocuments & Permission Hierarchy
Collaborators are tracked inside the `Folder` document via the `sharedWith` array:
```javascript
sharedWith: [{
  user: { type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId, ref: 'User' },
  permission: { type: String, enum: ['view', 'edit'], default: 'view' },
  addedAt: { type: Date, default: Date.now }
}]
```
Two discrete roles are enforced:
- **Viewer (`'view'`)**: Granted read privileges to preview, play, inspect, and download files residing within the folder.
- **Editor (`'edit'`)**: Granted full modification capabilities within the folder context, including uploading new assets directly into the shared folder, moving existing assets, and unfiling assets.

#### Sharing & Roster Mutation Controller
When `POST /api/folders/:id/share` is invoked, the controller verifies that `folder.user.toString() === req.user.id`, ensuring that only the original folder owner can modify access permissions. It performs an email lookup against the `User` collection. If the target exists and is distinct from the owner, it checks whether an entry already exists in `folder.sharedWith`. If present, it updates the permission property; otherwise, it pushes a new subdocument. Removing access occurs via `DELETE /api/folders/:id/share/:userId`, which filters the array by user ID and saves the document.

#### Shared Folder Discovery (`/api/folders/shared`)
The `GET /api/folders/shared` route returns all directories where the requesting user has been invited. It uses Mongoose query filtering on subdocument properties:
```javascript
Folder.find({ 'sharedWith.user': req.user.id }).populate('user', 'name email');
```
The server enriches each shared folder record with the owner's identity, the user's explicit permission level (`myPermission`), and an `isShared: true` boolean flag.

#### Client Collaborator Management UI
The `ShareFolderModal.js` component provides an invite interface. It displays the folder owner at the top of the roster adorned with a Shield icon and "Owner" badge. Each invited collaborator is rendered with their avatar initial, display name, email, permission level indicator, and a trash icon button. Clicking the delete icon prompts a `ConfirmModal` dialog to prevent accidental revocation of access.

