## Feature 8: Public File Sharing, Cryptographic Tokens & Link Protection

### 8.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub enables users to share individual media files with anyone outside the platform through unique, cryptographically random share links. Links can be optionally protected with salted bcrypt passwords and configured with automated time-based expirations.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Owner as File Owner
    participant API as /api/share
    participant LinkModel as ShareLink Model
    actor Public as Public Visitor
    participant ViewPage as /share/:token (React)

    Owner->>API: POST /api/share { fileId, fileType, password: "secret", expiresInDays: 7 }
    API->>API: crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex')
    API->>API: bcrypt.hash("secret", 10)
    API->>LinkModel: Save token, hashed password, expiresAt
    API-->>Owner: 201 Created { token, hasPassword: true, expiresAt }
    Owner->>Public: Distribute URL: https://app/share/<token>

    Public->>ViewPage: Visits URL in browser
    ViewPage->>API: GET /api/share/<token>
    alt Link Expired
        API-->>ViewPage: 410 Gone { message: 'Link expired' }
        ViewPage-->>Public: Render Error: 'Link Unavailable'
    else Password Required
        API-->>ViewPage: 401 Unauthorized { requirePassword: true }
        ViewPage-->>Public: Render Password Input Card
        Public->>ViewPage: Submits password
        ViewPage->>API: POST /api/share/<token>/verify { password }
        API->>API: bcrypt.compare(password, link.password)
        alt Password Correct
            API-->>ViewPage: 200 OK { success: true }
            ViewPage->>API: GET /api/share/<token>?p=secret
            API->>API: link.viewCount += 1; link.save()
            API-->>ViewPage: Serve raw file stream (res.sendFile)
            ViewPage-->>Public: Render Media Preview + Download Button
        else Password Incorrect
            API-->>ViewPage: 401 Unauthorized { message: 'Invalid password' }
            ViewPage-->>Public: Display 'Incorrect password' error
        end
    end
```

### 8.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Cryptographic Token Generation & Hashing
When creating a share link via `POST /api/share`, the system generates an unguessable 64-character URL-safe token using Node.js's native cryptographic library:
```javascript
const token = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex');
```
If the user specifies a password in `ShareModal`, the controller generates a bcrypt salt and hashes the plaintext password before storage. If an expiration timeframe is selected (1, 7, or 30 days), it calculates `expiresAt` by adding days to `new Date()`. The resulting `ShareLink` record stores `fileId`, `fileType`, `user`, `token`, `password`, `expiresAt`, and `viewCount: 0`.

#### The Public File Serving Engine (`GET /api/share/:token`)
When a visitor accesses the public file endpoint, the server performs validation checks:
1. **Link Existence**: Resolves `ShareLink.findOne({ token: req.params.token })`. If absent, returns `404 Not Found`.
2. **Expiration Enforcement**: Compares `link.expiresAt` against `new Date()`. If expired, returns `410 Gone`.
3. **Password Interception**: If `link.password` is truthy, the endpoint verifies whether a password parameter is provided. If missing or invalid, it returns a `401 Unauthorized` response with `{ requirePassword: true }`.
4. **View Tracking & Delivery**: Increments `link.viewCount += 1`, persists the update, locates the original file on disk, and pipes the binary stream using Express's `res.sendFile(path.resolve(file.path))`.

#### Dedicated Public UI: `SharePageView.js`
The public view page operates as a standalone micro-app that requires no user authentication. It manages an explicit four-state machine:
- `loading`: Displays an animated loading spinner.
- `password_required`: Displays a card featuring a Lock icon, description, password input, and unlock button. Submitting calls `POST /api/share/:token/verify`.
- `loaded`: Renders a full preview of the asset (responsive `<img>` for images, HTML5 `<video controls>` for video files, or document card for Office/PDF files), metadata badges (file size, format tag), and a large download button.
- `error`: Displays an alert triangle icon with descriptive messaging if the link has been revoked or expired.

#### Share Management Dashboard
Users can audit their active share links via `GET /api/share/my-links`. The server enriches each link with the original file name and masks the password (returning only a `password: true/false` flag). Users can revoke links anytime via `DELETE /api/share/:id`.

