## Feature 10: Bulk Operations, Multi-Select Engine & Streaming ZIP Archival

### 10.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub includes a multi-selection engine that enables power users to batch-manage their assets. Users can select multiple arbitrary files across categories, download them as a compressed ZIP archive streamed on-the-fly, or perform batch deletions.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["User clicks Multi-Select Toggle Button"] --> B["Enable Selection Mode (isSelecting = true)"]
    B --> C["User clicks media cards or 'Select All'"]
    C --> D["selectedFiles Set tracks File IDs"]
    D --> E["Floating Selection Bar mounts at screen bottom"]
    
    subgraph Bulk Actions
        E -- Click 'Download ZIP' --> F["Group Selected IDs by mediaType"]
        E -- Click 'Delete' --> G["Prompt ConfirmModal"]
        E -- Click 'Cancel' --> H["clearSelection(): Empty Set & Exit Mode"]
    end
    
    subgraph ZIP Streaming Pipeline
        F --> I["POST /api/:type/download-zip { imageIds: [...] }"]
        I --> J["archiver('zip', { zlib: { level: 9 } })"]
        J --> K["Set HTTP Headers: Content-Type: application/zip, Content-Disposition: attachment"]
        K --> L["Pipe archive stream directly to Express res"]
        L --> M["Iterate files -> archive.file(file.path, { name: file.originalName })"]
        M --> N["archive.finalize()"]
        N --> O["Browser triggers native file download (images.zip)"]
    end
    
    subgraph Batch Delete Pipeline
        G -- Confirmed --> P["Execute Promise.all([ DELETE calls for each selected ID ])"]
        P --> Q["Clear Selection Set & Refresh Gallery"]
        Q --> R["Toast: 'X files deleted'"]
    end
```

### 10.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Multi-Select State Machine
Multi-select functionality is coordinated in `ImageUploadPage.js` using an ES6 `Set` stored in the `selectedFiles` state variable. Using a `Set` ensures $O(1)$ constant-time lookup performance when evaluating whether an individual card is checked:
```javascript
const toggleFileSelect = (id) => {
  setSelectedFiles((prev) => {
    const next = new Set(prev);
    next.has(id) ? next.delete(id) : next.add(id);
    return next;
  });
};
```
When selection mode is engaged, clicking any media card toggles its membership in the `selectedFiles` Set instead of launching the preview modal. A floating action bar (`.selection-bar`) slides up from the bottom of the viewport as soon as `selectedFiles.size > 0`.

#### On-the-Fly ZIP Streaming with Archiver
The ZIP download functionality streams compressed archives directly from memory using the `archiver` library. The client divides selected items into three type buckets: `images`, `videos`, and `documents`. For each populated bucket, it issues a request to `/api/:type/download-zip`:
```javascript
router.post('/download-zip', protect, async (req, res) => {
  const { imageIds } = req.body;
  const images = await Image.find({ _id: { $in: imageIds }, user: req.user.id });

  res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/zip');
  res.setHeader('Content-Disposition', 'attachment; filename=images.zip');

  const archive = archiver('zip', { zlib: { level: 9 } });
  archive.pipe(res);

  for (const img of images) {
    if (fs.existsSync(img.path)) {
      archive.file(img.path, { name: img.originalName });
    }
  }
  archive.finalize();
});
```
By setting `zlib: { level: 9 }`, the server applies maximum compression. Piping the archive stream directly into the Express `res` object streams chunks to the client as they compress, maintaining a negligible server memory footprint even when archiving multi-hundred-megabyte batches.

#### Bulk Delete Execution
Clicking "Delete" in the floating selection bar opens a `ConfirmModal` dialog. Upon confirmation, the application maps every selected file to its corresponding DELETE endpoint and fires them concurrently using `Promise.all`:
```javascript
await Promise.all(
  items.map((item) => {
    const endpoint = item.mediaType === 'video' ? 'videos' : item.mediaType === 'document' ? 'documents' : 'images';
    return fetch(`${API_URL}/api/${endpoint}/${item._id}`, {
      method: 'DELETE',
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
    });
  })
);
```
Once complete, the selection is cleared, and the gallery refreshes.

