## Feature 12: AI-Powered Context-Aware Chatbot Assistant

### 12.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub integrates an AI assistant powered by OpenAI's GPT-3.5 Turbo model. Accessible via `/api/chatbot`, it provides users with natural language assistance, troubleshooting guidance, and contextual navigation advice for managing their files.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User in Chatbot Modal
    participant ChatAPI as POST /api/chatbot
    participant OpenAISDK as OpenAI API Client
    participant Fallback as Local Fallback Engine

    User->>ChatAPI: POST { message: "How do I download multiple files at once?" }
    ChatAPI->>OpenAISDK: openai.chat.completions.create(model: "gpt-3.5-turbo", messages: [...])
    
    alt OpenAI Service Available
        OpenAISDK-->>ChatAPI: AI Response String
        ChatAPI-->>User: 200 OK { success: true, response, suggestions, isAI: true }
    else OpenAI Rate Limit / Network Failure / Missing Key
        OpenAISDK-->>ChatAPI: Error Exception
        ChatAPI->>Fallback: Select predefined contextual response
        Fallback-->>ChatAPI: Static Guidance Response
        ChatAPI-->>User: 200 OK { success: true, response, suggestions, isAI: false }
    end
    
    User->>User: Render Message Bubble & Follow-up Suggestion Chips
```

### 12.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### The Chatbot Route Controller
Implemented in `backend/routes/chatbotRoutes.js`, the chatbot endpoint accepts user messages over an authenticated connection. The controller initializes the official `OpenAI` client SDK, passing `process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY`. It dispatches chat completion requests configured with specific constraints:
```javascript
const completion = await openai.chat.completions.create({
  model: 'gpt-3.5-turbo',
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'system',
      content: 'You are a helpful AI assistant for a file storage application named GalleryHub. Guide users on uploading, organizing into folders, sharing files, and editing images.',
    },
    { role: 'user', content: message },
  ],
  max_tokens: 200,
  temperature: 0.7,
});
```

#### Dual-Path Fallback Resilience
Because cloud AI services can experience network latency, API key exhaustion, or outages, the controller wraps the OpenAI call in an internal try-catch block. If the OpenAI request fails, the API gracefully falls back:
```javascript
catch (error) {
  console.log('ChatGPT failed, using fallback:', error.message);
  response = "Hello! I'm here to help you with file management. How can I assist you today?";
  isAI = false;
}
```
The API returns a 200 status code regardless, delivering the response alongside an `isAI: boolean` indicator and a curated array of interactive suggestion chips:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "response": "...",
  "suggestions": [
    "How do I upload files?",
    "Show me my storage usage",
    "What file types are supported?"
  ],
  "isAI": true
}
```
This guarantees that the chatbot interface remains responsive and helpful even without an active OpenAI API key.

