## Feature 13: User Profile, Account Security, Storage Quotas & Danger Zone Operations

### 13.1 Overview & Architecture
The account management subsystem provides tools for profile editing, custom avatar uploads, password changes, real-time storage quota tracking, and high-consequence administrative operations (the "Danger Zone").

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Settings Navigation (/gallery -> settings tab)"] --> B{"Settings Sub-Section"}
    
    B -- "profile" --> C["Profile Edit Sub-Page"]
    B -- "password" --> D["Password Change Sub-Page"]
    B -- "main" --> E["Main Settings Hub"]
    
    subgraph Profile Management
        C --> C1["Upload Custom Avatar -> PUT /api/users/profile/picture"]
        C --> C2["Update Name & Email -> PUT /api/users/profile"]
    end
    
    subgraph Password Security
        D --> D1["Validate Current Password (bcrypt.compare)"]
        D --> D2["Enforce 6-Char Min & Confirmation Match"]
        D --> D3["Hash New Password via Pre-Save Hook"]
    end
    
    subgraph Storage Quota Tracking
        E --> E1["Aggregate Total Size: allMedia.reduce(size)"]
        E1 --> E2["Compare Against 500MB Limit"]
        E2 --> E3["Render Dynamic Bar: Green <50%, Yellow 50-80%, Red >80%"]
    end
    
    subgraph Danger Zone Operations
        E --> F["Click 'Delete All Files'"]
        F --> G["Prompt ConfirmModal Warning"]
        G -- Confirmed --> H["Execute Parallel Cascade Deletion Across All Collections"]
        H --> I["Reclaim Storage Quota to 0 MB"]
    end
```

### 13.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Profile Modifications & LocalStorage Synchronization
Users can update their personal information on the profile editing sub-page. Submitting modifications dispatches a `PUT /api/users/profile` request containing `{ name, email }`. The controller checks `User.findById(req.user._id)`, applies changes, and saves the record. On the client side, successful updates update both React state and the serialized `localStorage` session cache:
```javascript
const stored = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('userInfo'));
stored.name = data.name;
stored.email = data.email;
localStorage.setItem('userInfo', JSON.stringify(stored));
```

#### Avatar Ingestion Pipeline
Clicking the user's avatar opens a hidden file input accepting `image/*`. The selected file is uploaded via `PUT /api/users/profile/picture` using a dedicated Multer disk storage engine configured to save avatars into `backend/uploads/` with a unique `profile-${Date.now()}` prefix. The user document's `profilePicture` field is updated with the new filename, which renders across the navigation header, settings menu, and collaboration modals.

#### Password Verification & Modification
Changing an account password requires entering the current password alongside the new password twice. The backend controller performs two-step validation:
```javascript
const user = await User.findById(req.user._id).select('+password');
if (await user.matchPassword(req.body.currentPassword)) {
  user.password = req.body.newPassword;
  await user.save();
} else {
  return res.status(401).json({ message: 'Incorrect current password.' });
}
```
Assigning `user.password = req.body.newPassword` flags the field as modified, automatically triggering the Mongoose pre-save hook to hash the new password with bcrypt before writing to the database.

#### Dynamic Storage Quota Analytics
GalleryHub tracks storage consumption against a defined ceiling of 500 MB (`500 * 1024 * 1024` bytes). The client calculates real-time usage across all loaded assets:
```javascript
const totalSize = allMedia.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (item.size || 0), 0);
const usagePercent = Math.min((totalSize / STORAGE_QUOTA) * 100, 100);
const quotaColor = usagePercent > 80 ? '#ea4335' : usagePercent > 50 ? '#fbbc04' : '#34a853';
```
The storage quota bar dynamically adjusts its width percentage and color (green for healthy capacity, amber for moderate usage, red for approaching capacity), providing an at-a-glance visualization of storage usage.

#### The Danger Zone: Full Content Eradication
The Danger Zone houses the "Delete All Files" action. To prevent catastrophic accidental data loss, clicking the button presents a `ConfirmModal` dialog. Confirming executes batch deletion across all collections, unlinks the physical files, resets local state arrays to empty, and reclaims all consumed storage.

