## Feature 14: System-Aware Dynamic Theme Engine & Custom Accent Color Customizer

### 14.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub includes a comprehensive theming system that supports three operational modes: System, Light, and Dark. In System mode, it listens to OS-level theme preferences in real-time. Additionally, users can personalize their UI with six custom accent colors.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Theme Resolution Logic
        A["themeMode State ('system' | 'light' | 'dark')"]
        B["systemIsDark State (window.matchMedia listener)"]
        A & B --> C{"Resolve darkMode Boolean"}
        C --> D["Apply/Remove '.dark' Class on document.documentElement"]
        D --> E["CSS Variables Switch Colors (--bg, --surface, --text, --border)"]
    end

    subgraph Accent Color Customization
        F["User selects Accent Color (e.g., #a855f7)"] --> G["localStorage.setItem('settings_accentColor', color)"]
        G --> H["document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--primary', color)"]
        H --> I["Buttons, Highlights, Badges & Focus Rings Instantly Re-Skin"]
    end
```

### 14.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### Three-Tier Theme Resolution Matrix
Theme state is initialized in `App.js` with fallback to `localStorage`:
```javascript
const [themeMode, setThemeMode] = useState(() => localStorage.getItem('themeMode') || 'system');
const [systemIsDark, setSystemIsDark] = useState(
  () => window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches
);
const darkMode = themeMode === 'system' ? systemIsDark : themeMode === 'dark';
```

#### Real-Time OS Preference Listener
To react when a user switches their operating system theme (e.g., automated sunset dark mode transitions), `App.js` establishes a persistent `MediaQueryList` event listener:
```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  const mediaQuery = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)');
  const handleChange = (e) => setSystemIsDark(e.matches);

  if (mediaQuery.addEventListener) {
    mediaQuery.addEventListener('change', handleChange);
  } else {
    mediaQuery.addListener(handleChange);
  }
  return () => mediaQuery.removeEventListener('change', handleChange);
}, []);
```
Whenever `darkMode` updates, a secondary `useEffect` toggles the `.dark` class on the root HTML element: `document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', darkMode)`.

#### CSS Variable Architecture
The styling system relies on CSS custom properties declared in `index.css`:
```css
:root {
  --bg: #f8fafc;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --text: #0f172a;
  --text-secondary: #64748b;
  --border: #e2e8f0;
  --primary: #4285f4;
  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
}

html.dark {
  --bg: #0b0f17;
  --surface: #131b2e;
  --text: #f8fafc;
  --text-secondary: #94a3b8;
  --border: #1e293b;
  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
}
```
All UI components bind their backgrounds, borders, and typography to these CSS variables, enabling instant, flicker-free theme switches across the entire application.

#### Runtime Accent Color Injection
Users can choose from six vibrant accent color presets:
- Google Blue (`#4285f4`)
- Royal Purple (`#a855f7`)
- Hot Pink (`#ec4899`)
- Emerald Green (`#34a853`)
- Sunset Amber (`#fbbc04`)
- Crimson Red (`#ea4335`)

Selecting a swatch persists the hex string to `localStorage` under `settings_accentColor` and applies it dynamically at runtime:
```javascript
document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--primary', color);
```
Primary buttons, active filter tabs, selection checkboxes, slider tracks, and focus indicators instantly update to match the selected color.

