## Feature 15: Guided Onboarding Tour, Skeleton Shimmer Loading & UI Polish

### 15.1 Overview & Architecture
GalleryHub incorporates user onboarding and visual polish mechanisms to ensure an intuitive user experience. An automated walkthrough guides first-time users through the interface, while shimmer skeleton cards prevent layout shift during data loading.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Onboarding Engine
        A["App Mounts in Browser"] --> B{"Check localStorage('onboardingCompleted')"}
        B -- Null / False --> C["Initialize OnboardingTour (intro.js-react)"]
        B -- True --> D["Bypass Tour"]
        
        C --> E["Step 1: Welcome & Brand Logo"]
        E --> F["Step 2: Upload Action Button"]
        F --> G["Step 3: Gallery Views & Tabs"]
        G --> H["Step 4: Folder Navigation"]
        H --> I["Step 5: Activity Audit Feed"]
        I --> J["Step 6: User Profile & Settings"]
        J --> K["Set localStorage('onboardingCompleted', 'true')"]
    end

    subgraph Skeleton Shimmer Pipeline
        L["Data Fetching Initiated (loading = true)"] --> M["Render SkeletonGrid (count = 8)"]
        M --> N["Generate 8 SkeletonCard Items"]
        N --> O["CSS Linear Gradient Shimmer Animation (2s infinite)"]
        O --> P["Data Resolves -> Smooth Cross-Fade to Live Media Cards"]
    end
```

### 15.2 Deep Technical Implementation

#### The Guided Onboarding System (`OnboardingTour.js`)
First-time user onboarding is built using `intro.js` and `intro.js-react`. The `OnboardingTour` component renders on the main dashboard. It reads `localStorage.getItem('onboardingCompleted')`. If absent, it initiates a 6-step guided walkthrough after a 1000ms delay to allow dashboard data to mount:
1. `.brand-logo`: Welcome banner explaining the purpose of GalleryHub.
2. `.bottom-dock-upload`: Points to the prominent upload button.
3. `.category-tabs`: Explains filtering across images, videos, and documents.
4. `.quick-folders-section`: Demonstrates folder organization and drag-and-drop targets.
5. `.activity-feed-container`: Introduces the real-time operational audit log.
6. `.user-profile-menu`: Shows how to configure settings, themes, and account security.

The tour validates that target DOM elements are present before advancing steps to prevent errors on different viewport sizes. When the user completes or dismisses the tour, it writes `localStorage.setItem('onboardingCompleted', 'true')`.

#### Shimmer Skeleton Architecture (`SkeletonCard.js`)
To prevent Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) during initial data fetching, GalleryHub renders animated skeleton loading cards via `SkeletonGrid`. The component renders placeholder cards matching the 4:3 aspect ratio of live media cards, complete with simulated text lines for the filename and date metadata.

The loading animation is driven by a CSS gradient keyframe animation in `SkeletonCard.css`:
```css
.skeleton-shimmer {
  background: linear-gradient(
    90deg,
    var(--surface) 0%,
    var(--border) 50%,
    var(--surface) 100%
  );
  background-size: 200% 100%;
  animation: shimmer 1.8s infinite ease-in-out;
}

@keyframes shimmer {
  0% { background-position: -200% 0; }
  100% { background-position: 200% 0; }
}
```
This produces a smooth, shimmering wave effect that communicates loading progress to the user.

#### Micro-Interactions & Animation Utilities
The application utilizes a suite of CSS keyframe animation utility classes:
- `.animate-fade-in`: 0.25s opacity transition from 0 to 1 for content swapping.
- `.animate-slide-up`: Modals and floating action bars smoothly translate from `translateY(20px)` to `translateY(0)`.
- `.animate-slide-down`: Dropdown context menus slide downward smoothly.
- `.animate-scale-in`: Used for confirmation dialogues, scaling from `scale(0.95)` to `scale(1)`.

